{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1473973-new-compact-hard-silly-concept","id":1473973,"title":"New Compact: HARD [Silly Concept]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-04T07:29:15-08:00","id":1473973,"title":"New Compact: HARD [Silly Concept]","content":"So it had been a while since I wrote a new Hunter org (mostly because I am busy at updating some of my old groups and expand them into a quality STV material) but some time ago there was a discussion about &quot;how would a PETA like hunter compact look like&quot;, and this is my answer. I do not intent to take it too seriously- but I hope you will enjoy it!<br /> <br /> <b><i>Humans Against Radical Domestication</i></b><br /> <br /> Ask the common hunter what is the problem in the world, and they will probably give you a very simple answer- the monsters are the problem. For ages the darkness have preyed upon the innocents, lurking just outside the fire, just at the edge of the cave, just on the limit of your peripheral sight. It is waiting for the humans to let their guard down and sweep in, murdering and abusing and defiling all that is sacred. It is the duty of the hunters to fight the darkness, to keep it at bay, to make sure that the candle will keep burning against the horrors of the night. Fighting the monsters and reclaiming the night- that is the life of a hunter. That is the Vigil. Some may do compromises, sure- but at its essence, all hunters are driven to bring an end to the things which lurk in the night.<br /> <br /> HARD are not the common hunters, however.<br /> <br /> Founded in the US during the 80s, HARD was originally composed from a number of hunters who couldn't find their place among other compacts and cells. Most of them were somewhat experienced, having survived a few hunts going wrong. Others were pretty green, motivated by idealism after getting out alive from their first bump in the night. All, however, had one thing in common- they believed that the Vigil was not a solution. It was the problem. Here is the thing- the monsters were probably there before humanity, especially before humans around around and built their fancy cities, disrupting the local ecological systems and causing damage to how those entities have lived their lives. Worse, some humans even try to exploit the (super)natural resources for their own needs, further pushing monsters in a state they must attack humans in order to survive. That creature made out of fanged and eyes and broken wood? It is not that different from a polar bear starving in the north attacking human settlements. Reclaiming the night? You mean &quot;destroy the natural ecology which kept the so called monsters happy and safe in their natural environment&quot;. No, humans shouldn't try to take over monstrous territory- but to respect those strange children of Mother Earth and not take over their homes or destroy their younglings just because they are a &quot;threat&quot;. That's how species go extinct, you selfish bastard.<br /> <br /> During that time, HuFES was created- Humans For Ecological Safety. During that time, the compact was based mostly around explaining other hunters what they are doing wrong, using ecological models and attempting to define &quot;natural reservations&quot; for monsters to live freely. The problem they said, was human overpopulation- too many people taking too much territory where monsters originally lived, forcing them to enter the cities to find food and shelter. According to HuFES, the hunters were supposed to capture and release monsters back to the wilderness, and if some humans get killed in the process then it is something people just need to accept- especially when they get killed in the &quot;nests&quot; the monster calls home (monsters naturally only try to protect themselves, after all). As one may expect, the wider hunter community did not took HuFES' ideology kindly- many hunters saw them as either mislead, crazy, foolish, compromised or all of the above. Not many hunters have shown interest in their ideology- but those who did were very ideological and supportive for the cause. Still, HuFES was more or less isolated among the Vigilante society, with most hunters simply waiting for them to understand their own mistakes- or, more likely, get killed by them.<br /> <br /> And of course the more likely option was the one to take place.<br /> <br /> During the compact's one of many &quot;catch and release&quot; operation, the compact came into an ambush. Apparently, some of the &quot;freed&quot; vampires managed to crawl their way into the city without getting burned in the sun or starve into madness and explained his friends where do all the vampires get disappeared to. As one may imagine, the bloodsuckers didn't took it too kindly, and set up the compact just when they were about to save another lich from the &quot;reservation&quot; the hunters decided for the undead. Needless to say, it was blood bath- more than 2/3 of the compact were slaughtered, and one half of the survivors died from their wounds later on. That, by all accounts, should have been the end of the compact- and in a way, it was. This event made HuFES to understand that they were wrong- that it was too late to save the monsters. Sure, some of them can be returned to their natural place- but many have gone too corrupted, too domesticated in order to survive like their ancestors did. Those monsters can't be saved- the only thing which can be done is to end the misery of those poor domesticated species by putting an end for them, out of hope that new, more true and pure forms of monsters will rise to take their place.<br /> <br /> HuFES was no more. Now there was only HARD- Humans Against Radical Domestication.<br /> <br /> Strangely enough, HARD's new ideology made them more accepted among the Vigil- sure, they were still crazy people who talked nonsense about how &quot;monsters need to be protected&quot; and &quot;how humans corrupt innocent supernatural species&quot;, but in the end, the averaged HARD hunter got the job done, even if they were apologizing to the werewolf while putting a silver bullet in their head and then sobbing for half a hour later. HARD, in turn, have started to develop further their own ideology, telling their members how to identify which monster could be redeemed by returning it to nature and which had to be ended for its own good. After much debate, arguing and perhaps a member or two falling into slasherhood, HARD have managed to define for themselves which monsters were the problem- specifically, the more human ones. Where cryptids and spirits are just strange animals, vampires, ghosts and witches are examples for humanity corrupting the natural species, driving them into unnatural forms which depends of the human society in order to survive- or as they like to call it, &quot;Radical Domestication&quot;. Where most HARD members accept that they have to kill those poor monsters as it is too late to save them, after surviving for two decades some members have come to an interesting discovery- that some monsters can be redeemed. All that they need to do was to help them forget their humanity- cut loose the ties of a vampire with the mortal society, or keep a werewolf away from the human society, and they would slowly and surely return to their original, primal forms, ones which could probably survive on the wilderness and represent how they truly should exist. Sometimes, however, they need some &quot;help&quot; in order to return to such form- oh, sure, it may look like torture for an outside, but HARD know what they are doing, and that the pain the monster feels is simply them giving up on the corrupted effects of self domestication, and that they'll be happier this way. Lately, some of their members have even came in contact with some forms of those &quot;primal monsters&quot;, such as packs of great werewolves who deny the use of human societies or strange shadow birds who seem to host the bodies of the undead, and while unfortunately most of those contacts have ended with the death (a sacrifice which must be made), others have shown great interest in helping HARD to redeem the monsters from their sorrowful domestication- giving their support for HARD's efforts at saving the monsters from themselves.<br /> <br /> Of course, most hunters will be disgusted if they'll discover those actions and contacts- after all, while all monsters are dangerous, by removing their &quot;domestication&quot; those monsters will become true horrors which would ruin everything the Vigil is fighting for. But for HARD, it is simply means returning to the original form of living- there are too many humans, and people should accept their place within the natural order. The monsters are simply a part of nature, and only by reclaiming their primal forms they could be saved. Things will be better this way, you will see. The darkness was never humanity's property in the first place, after all. There is nothing for it to &quot;reclaim&quot; there. This is the source of all problems- currently, there are too many candles burning in the night.<br /> <br /> It is time to extinguish a few for the greater good.<br /> <br /> <b>Status:</b><br /> 0- You have just joined HARD, filled with ideological vigor and the need to save the monsters from themselves. You gain free Expression (Debates) or Science (Ecology) Specialty for free.<br /> 000- You have saved many lives in your quest to bring monsters back to their natural state and explaining other hunters why monsters act like they do. Other people in the compact are drawn for your actions and support you in your times of need. You gain Allies for 2 dots for free.<br /> 00000- You have personally helped monsters to reclaim their original glory, and take active part on the Anti Domestication secret projects which the compact manages. As such, you are one of the rare individuals who maintain connection with their &quot;monstrous allies&quot;. You gain Contacts for 3 dots for one monstrous faction which supports the goals of HARD (such as the Strix, the Predator Kings or even the forged spawn of a idigam)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T19:45:01-07:00","id":1508317,"title":"","content":"A new Cabal huh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}